            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0654" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.1 Polk, Frank L.:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-19T19:00:00+01:00">July 19, 1919—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3227. Arrival of Mr. Polk will necessitate issuance of new document of
                    appointment and full power for the Commissioners jointly to supersede that of
                    November 30, 1919 [<hi rendition="#italic">1918</hi>].<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d294-f1"/> It is believed that the wording used in the original
                    document will empower Commissioners to sign treaties with Bulgaria and
                    Turkey.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
